   line_ : matplotlib Artist\n 41 |         ROC Curve.\n 42 | \n 43 |     ax_ : matplotlib Axes\n 44 |         Axes with ROC Curve.\n 45 | \n 46 |     figure_ : matplotlib Figure\n 47 |         Figure containing the curve.\n 48 | \n 49 |     See Also\n 50 |     --------\n 51 |     roc_curve : Compute Receiver operating characteristic (ROC) curve.\n 52 |     plot_roc_curve : Plot Receiver operating characteristic (ROC) curve.\n 53 |     roc_auc_score : Compute the area under the ROC curve.\n 54 | \n 55 |     Examples\n 56 |     --------\n 57 |     >>> import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n 58 |     >>> import numpy as np\n 59 |     >>> from sklearn import metrics\n 60 |     >>> y = np.array([0, 0, 1, 1])\n 61 |     >>> pred = np.array([0.1, 0.4, 0.35, 0.8])\n 62 |     >>> fpr, tpr, thresholds = metrics.roc_curve(y, pred)\n 63 |     >>> roc_auc = metrics.auc(fpr, tpr)\n 64 |     >>> display = metrics.RocCurveDisplay(fpr=fpr, tpr=tpr, roc_auc=roc_auc,\\\n 65 |                                           estimator_name='example estimator')\n 66 |     >>> display.plot()\n 67 |     <...>\n 68 |     >>> plt.show()\n 69 |     \"\"\"\n 70 | \n 71 |     def __init__(self, *, fpr, tpr, roc_auc=None, estimator_name=None, pos_label=None):\n 72 |         self.estimator_name = estimator_name\n 73 |         self.fpr = fpr\n 74 |         self.tpr = tpr\n 75 |         self.roc_auc = roc_auc\n 76 |         self.pos_label = pos_label\n```\nHint: \nThe code for class `sklearn/metrics/_plot/roc_curve.py:RocCurveDisplay` is incomplete; search `sklearn/metrics/_plot/roc_curve.py:RocCurveDisplay` for the full content if needed.\n\nFound function `sklearn/metrics/_plot/base.py:_check_classifier_response_method`.\nSource: Retrieved entity using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n 6 | def _check_classifier_response_method(estimator, response_method):\n 7 |     \"\"\"Return prediction method from the response_method\n 8 | \n 9 |     Parameters\n10 |     ----------\n11 |     estimator: object\n12 |         C