stimators, it is instead recommended to use platform-independent int32 if\n901 |     we do not expect to index more 2B elements. Using fixed dtypes simplifies\n902 |     the handling of serialized models, e.g. to deploy a model fit on a 64-bit\n903 |     platform to a target 32-bit platform such as WASM/pyodide.\n904 |     \"\"\"\n905 |     # Currently this is implemented with simple hack that assumes that\n906 |     # following \"may be\" statements in the Array API spec always hold:\n907 |     # > The default integer data type should be the same across platforms, but\n908 |     # > the default may vary depending on whether Python is 32-bit or 64-bit.\n909 |     # > The default array index data type may be int32 on 32-bit platforms, but\n910 |     # > the default should be int64 otherwise.\n911 |     # https://data-apis.org/array-api/latest/API_specification/data_types.html#default-data-types\n912 |     # TODO: once sufficiently adopted, we might want to instead rely on the\n913 |     # newer inspection API: https://github.com/data-apis/array-api/issues/640\n914 |     return xp.asarray(0).dtype\n```\n\nFound file `sklearn/utils/_array_api.py`.\nSource: Retrieved entity using keyword search (bm25).\nHint: Search `sklearn/utils/_array_api.py` for the full content if needed.\n"}, {"content": "Let me also check the config handling since it's relevant to the Array API:\n\n<function=search_code_snippets>\n<parameter=search_terms>['get_config', 'set_config', 'array_api_dispatch']</parameter>\n", "role": "assistant", "tool_calls": null, "function_call": null}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "toolu_01", "name": "search_code_snippets", "content": "OBSERVATION:\nsklearn/_config.py:set_config\nsklearn/_config.py:config_context\nsklearn/utils/_array_api.py:get_namespace\nsklearn/utils/estimator_checks.py:check_array_api_input\nsklearn/utils/_array_api.py:_check_array_api_dispatch\nsklearn/utils/estimator_checks.py:check_array_api_input\nsklearn/utils/_array_api.py:get_namespa