g keyword search (bm25).\nHint: Search `asv_bench/benchmarks/libs.py` for the full content if needed.\n\n\n\n##Searching for term \"StringMethods._validate\"...\n### Search Result:\nFound function `pandas/core/strings/accessor.py:StringMethods._validate`.\nSource: Match found for entity name `_validate`.\n```\n221 | def _validate(data):\n222 |         \"\"\"\n223 |         Auxiliary function for StringMethods, infers and checks dtype of data.\n224 | \n225 |         This is a \"first line of defence\" at the creation of the StringMethods-\n226 |         object, and just checks that the dtype is in the\n227 |         *union* of the allowed types over all string methods below; this\n228 |         restriction is then refined on a per-method basis using the decorator\n229 |         @forbid_nonstring_types (more info in the corresponding docstring).\n230 | \n231 |         This really should exclude all series/index with any non-string values,\n232 |         but that isn't practical for performance reasons until we have a str\n233 |         dtype (GH 9343 / 13877)\n234 | \n235 |         Parameters\n236 |         ----------\n237 |         data : The content of the Series\n238 | \n239 |         Returns\n240 |         -------\n241 |         dtype : inferred dtype of data\n242 |         \"\"\"\n243 |         if isinstance(data, ABCMultiIndex):\n244 |             raise AttributeError(\n245 |                 \"Can only use .str accessor with Index, not MultiIndex\"\n246 |             )\n247 | \n248 |         # see _libs/lib.pyx for list of inferred types\n249 |         allowed_types = [\"string\", \"empty\", \"bytes\", \"mixed\", \"mixed-integer\"]\n250 | \n251 |         data = extract_array(data)\n252 | \n253 |         values = getattr(data, \"categories\", data)  # categorical / normal\n254 | \n255 |         inferred_dtype = lib.infer_dtype(values, skipna=True)\n256 | \n257 |         if inferred_dtype not in allowed_types:\n258 |             raise AttributeError(\"Can only use .str accessor with string values!\")\n259 |         return inferred_dtype\n```\n"}, {"content": "Based on my analysis, here are the relevant code locations that need to be modified to implement the requested feature:\n\n```\npandas/core/strings/accessor.py\nline: 257-258\nfunction: StringMethods._validate\n\npandas/core/dtypes/dtypes.py\nline: 771-772\nfunction: DatetimeTZDtype.str\n\npandas/core/dtypes/common.py\nline: 1776\nfunction: is_dtype_equal\n\npandas/core/internals/managers.py\nline: 2140-2166\nfunction: maybe_coerce_values\n\npandas/core/construction.py\nline: 425-487\nfunction: extract_array\n```\n\nThe main changes needed are focused on the `StringMethods._validate` function in `pandas/core/strings/accessor.py`. This is the key location where the error message needs to be updated to include the inferred dtype information.\n\n<function=finish>\n", "role": "assistant", "tool_calls": null, "function_call": null}], "tools": [{"type": "function", "function": {"name": "finish", "description": "Finish the interaction when the task is complete OR if the assistant cannot proceed further with the task."}}, {"type": "function", "function": {"name": "search_code_snippets", "description": "Searches the codebase to retrieve relevant code snippets based on given queries(terms or line numbers).\n** Note:\n- Either `search_terms` or `line_nums` must be provided to perform a search.\n- If `search_terms` are provided, it searches for code snippets based on each term:\n- If `line_nums` is provided, it searches for code snippets around the specified lines within the file defined by `file_path_or_pattern`.\n\n** Example Usage:\n# Search for code content contain keyword `order`, `bill`\nsearch_code_snippets(search_terms=[\"order\", \"bill\"])\n\n# Search for a class\nsearch_code_snippets(search_terms=[\"MyClass\"])\n\n# Search for context around specific lines (10 and 15) within a file\nsearch_code_snippets(line_nums=[10, 15], file_path_or_pattern='src/example.py')\n", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {"search_terms": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}, "description": "A list of names, keywords, or code snippets to search for within the codebase. This can include potential function names, class names, or general code fragments. Either `search_terms` or `line_nums` must be provided to perform a search."}, "line_nums": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "integer"}, "description": "Specific line numbers to locate code snippets within a specified file. Must be used alongside a valid `file_path_or_pattern`. Either `line_nums` or `search_terms` must be provided to perform a search."}, "file_path_or_pattern": {"type": "string", "description": "A glob pattern or specific file path used to filter search results to particular files or directories. Defaults to \"**/*.py\", meaning all Python files are searched by default. If `line_nums` are provided, this must specify a specific file path.", "default": "**/*.py"}}, "required": []}}}, {"type": "function", "function": {"name": "get_entity_contents", "description": "\nSearches the codebase to retrieve the complete implementations of specified entities based on the provided entity names. \nThe tool can handle specific entity queries such as function names, class names, or file paths.\n\n**Usage Example:**\n# Search for a specific function implementation\nget_entity_contents(['src/my_file.py:MyClass.func_name'])\n\n# Search for a file's complete content\nget_entity_contents(['src/my_file.py'])\n\n**Entity Name Format:**\n- To specify a function or class, use the format: `file_path:QualifiedName`\n  (e.g., 'src/helpers/math_helpers.py:MathUtils.calculate_sum').\n- To search for a file's content, use only the file path (e.g., 'src/my_file.py').\n", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {"entity_names": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}, "description": "A list of entity names to query. Each entity name can represent a function, class, or file. For functions or classes, the format should be 'file_path:QualifiedName' (e.g., 'src/helpers/math_helpers.py:MathUtils.calculate_sum'). For files, use just the file path (e.g., 'src/my_file.py')."}}, "required": ["entity_names"]}}}], "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 167189, "completion_tokens": 465}, "time": 111.30212187767029}]}}
{"instance_id": "pandas-dev__pandas-60526", "found_files": [["pandas/core/computation/expressions.py"]], "found_modules": [["pandas/core/computation/expressions.py:_evaluate_standard", "pandas/plotting/_matplotlib/core.py:holds_integer", "pandas/core/accessor.py:PandasDelegate._add_delegate_accessors._create_delegator_method", "asv_bench/benchmarks/inference.py:ToDatetimeFromIntsFloats", "pandas/io/formats/html.py:HTMLFormatter", "pandas/plotting/_matplotlib/core.py:MPLPlot", "pandas/core/computation/expressions.py:_evaluate_numexpr", "pandas/plotting/_matplotlib/hist.py:KdePlot", "pandas/core/indexes/datetimelike.py:DatetimeIndexOpsMixin", "asv_bench/benchmarks/series_methods.py:Mode", "asv_bench/benchmarks/frame_methods.py:ToString", "pandas/core/computation/expressions.py:evaluate", "pandas/core/computation/expressions.py:_can_use_numexpr", "pandas/_typing.py:SequenceNotStr", "asv_bench/benchmarks/strings.py:Methods", "pandas/io/parquet.py:BaseImpl", "asv_bench/benchmarks/rolling.py:EWMMethods", "pandas/plotting/_matplotlib/boxplot.py:BoxPlot", "scripts/validate_docstrings.py:PandasDocstring"]], "found_entities": [["pandas/core/computation/expressions.py:_evaluate_standard", "pandas/plotting/_matplotlib/core.py:holds_integer", "pandas/core/accessor.py:PandasDelegate._add_delegate_accessors._create_delegator_method.f", "asv_bench/benchmarks/inference.py:ToDatetimeFromIntsFloats.time_sec_uint64", "pandas/io/formats/html.py:HTMLFormatter._get_columns_formatted_values", "pandas/plotting/_matplotlib/core.py:MPLPlot.orientation", "pandas/core/computation/expressions.py:_evaluate_numexpr", "pandas/plotting/_matplotlib/hist.py:KdePlot._kind", "pandas/core/indexes/datetimelike.py:DatetimeIndexOpsMixin._formatter_func", "pandas/plotting/_matplotlib/hist.py:KdePlot.orientation", "asv_bench/benchmarks/series_methods.py:Mode.time_mode", "asv_bench/benchmarks/frame_methods.py:ToString.time_to_string_floats", "pandas/core/computation/expressions.py:evaluate", "pandas/core/compu