ved code content using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n10956 | def corr(\n10957 |         self,\n10958 |         method: CorrelationMethod = \"pearson\",\n10959 |         min_periods: int = 1,\n10960 |         numeric_only: bool = False,\n10961 |     ) -> DataFrame:\n10962 |         \"\"\"\n10963 |         Compute pairwise correlation of columns, excluding NA/null values.\n10964 | \n10965 |         Parameters\n10966 |         ----------\n10967 |         method : {'pearson', 'kendall', 'spearman'} or callable\n10968 |             Method of correlation:\n10969 | \n10970 |             * pearson : standard correlation coefficient\n10971 |             * kendall : Kendall Tau correlation coefficient\n10972 |             * spearman : Spearman rank correlation\n10973 |             * callable: callable with input two 1d ndarrays\n10974 |                 and returning a float. Note that the returned matrix from corr\n10975 |                 will have 1 along the diagonals and will be symmetric\n10976 |                 regardless of the callable's behavior.\n10977 |         min_periods : int, optional\n10978 |             Minimum number of observations required per pair of columns\n10979 |             to have a valid result. Currently only available for Pearson\n10980 |             and Spearman correlation.\n10981 |         numeric_only : bool, default False\n10982 |             Include only `float`, `int` or `boolean` data.\n10983 | \n10984 |             .. versionadded:: 1.5.0\n10985 | \n10986 |             .. versionchanged:: 2.0.0\n10987 |                 The default value of ``numeric_only`` is now ``False``.\n10988 | \n10989 |         Returns\n10990 |         -------\n10991 |         DataFrame\n10992 |             Correlation matrix.\n10993 | \n10994 |         See Also\n10995 |         --------\n10996 |         DataFrame.corrwith : Compute pairwise correlation with another\n10997 |             DataFrame or Series.\n10998 |         Series.corr : Compute the correlation between two Series.\n10999 | \n11000 |         Notes\n11001 |         -----\n11002 |         Pearson, Kendall and Spearman correlation are currently computed using pairwise complete observations.\n11003 | \n11004 |         * `Pearson correlation coefficient <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pearson_correlation_coefficient>`_\n11005 |         * `Kendall rank correlation coefficient <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kendall_rank_correlation_coefficient>`_\n11006 |         * `Spearman's rank correlation coefficient <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spearman%27s_rank_correlation_coefficient>`_\n11007 | \n11008 |         Examples\n11009 |         --------\n11010 |         >>> def histogram_intersection(a, b):\n11011 |         ...     v = np.minimum(a, b).sum().round(decimals=1)\n11012 |         ...     return v\n11013 |         >>> df = pd.DataFrame(\n11014 |         ...     [(0.2, 0.3), (0.0, 0.6), (0.6, 0.0), (0.2, 0.1)],\n11015 |         ...     columns=[\"dogs\", \"cats\"],\n11016 |         ... )\n11017 |         >>> df.corr(method=histogram_intersection)\n11018 |               dogs  cats\n11019 |         dogs   1.0   0.3\n11020 |         cats   0.3   1.0\n11021 | \n11022 |         >>> df = pd.DataFrame(\n11023 |         ...     [(1, 1), (2, np.nan), (np.nan, 3), (4, 4)], columns=[\"dogs\", \"cats\"]\n11024 |         ... )\n11025 |         >>> df.corr(min_periods=3)\n11026 |               dogs  cats\n11027 |         dogs   1.0   NaN\n11028 |         cats   NaN   1.0\n11029 |         \"\"\"  # noqa: E501\n11030 |         data = self._get_numeric_data() if numeric_only else self\n11031 |         cols = data.columns\n11032 |         idx = cols.copy()\n11033 |         mat = data.to_numpy(dtype=float, na_value=np.nan, copy=False)\n11034 | \n11035 |         if method == \"pearson\":\n11036 |             correl = libalgos.nancorr(mat, minp=min_periods)\n11037 |         elif method == \"spearman\":\n11038 |             correl = libalgos.nancorr_spearman(mat, minp=min_periods)\n11039 |    