      decimals : int, dict, Series\n10831 |             Number of decimal places to round each column to. If an int is\n10832 |             given, round each column to the same number of places.\n10833 |             Otherwise dict and Series round to variable numbers of places.\n10834 |             Column names should be in the keys if `decimals` is a\n10835 |             dict-like, or in the index if `decimals` is a Series. Any\n10836 |             columns not included in `decimals` will be left as is. Elements\n10837 |             of `decimals` which are not columns of the input will be\n10838 |             ignored.\n10839 |         *args\n10840 |             Additional keywords have no effect but might be accepted for\n10841 |             compatibility with numpy.\n10842 |         **kwargs\n10843 |             Additional keywords have no effect but might be accepted for\n10844 |             compatibility with numpy.\n10845 | \n10846 |         Returns\n10847 |         -------\n10848 |         DataFrame\n10849 |             A DataFrame with the affected columns rounded to the specified\n10850 |             number of decimal places.\n10851 | \n10852 |         See Also\n10853 |         --------\n10854 |         numpy.around : Round a numpy array to the given number of decimals.\n10855 |         Series.round : Round a Series to the given number of decimals.\n10856 | \n10857 |         Notes\n10858 |         -----\n10859 |         For values exactly halfway between rounded decimal values, pandas rounds\n10860 |         to the nearest even value (e.g. -0.5 and 0.5 round to 0.0, 1.5 and 2.5\n10861 |         round to 2.0, etc.).\n10862 | \n10863 |         Examples\n10864 |         --------\n10865 |         >>> df = pd.DataFrame(\n10866 |         ...     [(0.21, 0.32), (0.01, 0.67), (0.66, 0.03), (0.21, 0.18)],\n10867 |         ...     columns=[\"dogs\", \"cats\"],\n10868 |         ... )\n10869 |         >>> df\n10870 |             dogs  cats\n10871 |         0  0.21  0.32\